course: dictionary
lesson: 2693
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word difference has three everyday meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. In a sum, difference means how much bigger one number is than another. «The difference between 14 and 9 is 5», so you subtract the smaller number from the bigger one.
explain: When you spot the differences between two pictures, difference means a way in which the two things are not the same. «Find the difference» in a class task asks you to look for what changes between them. If you can swap in the words not the same and the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: To make a difference means to change something, often for the better. «Our volunteers make a difference to the park.» Make no difference is different again: «It makes no difference to me» means it does not matter. Read the whole phrase, not just the word difference, to find its meaning.
fact: Difference, in maths, is how much bigger one number is than another, and you find it by subtracting.
fact: A difference is a way in which two things are not the same.
fact: To make a difference means to change something, often for the better.
fact: «It makes no difference» means it does not matter.
fact: In science, differences between materials help you sort and test them; «The difference is whether new substances are made» shows that cooking and burning make atoms join up in new ways.
exercise: «Jobs are not spread evenly: one town might have 8 in 100 unemployed and another 3 in 100.» What is the difference between these two numbers? | 11 | 8 | *5 | 2
exercise: Mr Hale says, «Spot the differences between these two pictures.» What does he want you to find? | Two pictures in colour | A new picture to draw | *Ways in which the two pictures are not the same | Two pictures that are alike
exercise: «Helping a friend with your own sacrifice is different from lying for them — know the difference.» What does know the difference mean? | Know the answer to a sum | *Know how the two things are not the same | Forget what is right | Tell your friend a lie
test: Maya scored 14 in a game and Sam scored 9. What is the difference between their scores? | 4 | *5 | 6 | 23
test: «It makes no difference to me whether we go now or later.» What does makes no difference mean? | It is a sum with a difference | It is a big change for the better | It is the best choice of all | *It does not matter either way
exam: Which meaning of difference is right for «Volunteers can make a difference to a town»? | Spot a picture that is wrong | *Change something, often for the better | Two things that are not the same | A number found by subtracting
